statement:
Let $X=\operatorname{Spec}R$ be nonempty, reduced, Noetherian, complete strictly henselian local, with residue field $k$ and dimension $d$, and let $V\subseteq X$ be a dense affine open [def-weil-affine-spectrum, def-pc-reduced-scheme, def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring, def-weil-pbc-adically-complete-ring, def-weil-pbc-henselian-terminology, def-weil-residue-field, def-weil-pbc-krull-dimension-ring, def-weil-open-immersion]. Fix a prime $\ell$ invertible in $R$ and $L\geq1$. There exist a complete discrete valuation ring $C$ with residue field $k$ and invertible $\ell$, Noetherian strictly henselian local schemes $T,T_0$, local maps
$$X\xrightarrow{a}T\xleftarrow{b}T_0,$$
an affine open $W\subseteq T$, and an $L$-truncated hypercover $T_\bullet\to T$ for the topology of $\ell'$-alterations [def-per-prime-to-ell-alteration-topology], such that:
(1) $a^{-1}W=V$, all closed residue field maps identify with $k$, and $\dim T_0=d$;
(2) $T_0$ is the strict henselization at a geometric point of a scheme of finite type over $\operatorname{Spec}C$ [def-weil-pbc-strict-henselization-limit, def-weil-finite-type-morphism];
(3) dominant reduced pullbacks $X_\bullet\to X$ and $(T_0)_\bullet\to T_0$ are $L$-truncated hypercovers for the topology of $\ell'$-alterations; dominant reduced pullback means the reduced union of components of the ordinary fibre product dominating a component of the new base;
(4) for each map $a,b$, every $0\leq i\leq L$, and every geometric point over the closed point on the pulled-back $i$th level, both source and target strict localizations are regular, the reduced complements of the inverse images of $W$ are strict normal crossings divisors, and target branch equations $f_1,\ldots,f_r$ pull back to source branch equations with linearly independent classes in its maximal ideal modulo its square [def-weil-regular-scheme, def-trf-strict-normal-crossings-boundary]. Empty boundaries are allowed.
A hypercover here is an augmented simplicial diagram whose maps to matching objects are covers, using dominant reduced fibre products. A discrete valuation ring means a Noetherian local domain of dimension one with principal maximal ideal; completeness means completeness for powers of that ideal. No equality $\dim T=d$ is asserted.
